---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="What Hum Jaise collects (very little) and why.">
  <PageIntro title="Privacy, in plain words" urdu="رازداری، سیدھے لفظوں میں">
    <p>We collect as little as we can. Here's exactly what that means.</p>
  </PageIntro>

  <div class="wrap privacy prose">
    <h2>Just visiting</h2>
    <p>
      No tracking, no analytics, no advertising and no cookies. Our fonts are stored on this site, so
      your browser doesn't contact Google or anyone else to show them. Like almost every website, our
      host (Netlify) may keep basic technical logs, such as IP addresses, for security.
    </p>

    <h2>Reading comfort settings</h2>
    <p>
      If you change text size, spacing, theme, movement or the light pattern, that choice is saved in
      your own browser so it's remembered next time. It never leaves your device. Clearing your browser
      data removes it.
    </p>

    <h2>If you write to us</h2>
    <p>
      The form only needs your message. A way to reply is optional. Messages are stored by Netlify Forms
      and read by the small group who run Hum Jaise. We don't publish, sell or share them. We won't quote
      any part of your message anywhere without asking you first.
    </p>
    <p>
      We can't promise complete anonymity. No website can. Please leave out names and details that could
      identify you or other people. If you'd like a message deleted, write to us again and say so.
    </p>

    <h2>Later on</h2>
    <p>
      If we add accounts or discussions, we'll update this page before they open, and explain what
      changes in plain words.
    </p>
    <p class="note">Last updated October 2026.</p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .privacy h2 { font-size: var(--step-2); margin: var(--space-4) 0 var(--space-2); }
  .privacy h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
</style>
